[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4185740393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170#issuecomment-4185740393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118170","id":4185740393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75fVRp","user":{"login":"mashumafi","id":1059099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTkwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1059099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi","html_url":"https://github.com/mashumafi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T00:07:54Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T00:07:54Z","body":"I see compatibility test failed for mono. I know this feature in general can be risky and break backward compatibility. One example is that using the numbers from json results that were a double and are now an int would impact arithmetic operators. Open to discussion on alternative ideas too","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4185740393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4185933442","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170#issuecomment-4185933442","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118170","id":4185933442,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75gEaC","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T01:24:09Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T01:24:09Z","body":"The JSON format [does not make a distinction between integers and floating point numbers](https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/reference/numeric#integer), so `1.0` is a valid way to represent an integer, and `1` is a valid way to represent a floating point number.\r\n\r\nThere are plenty of JSON serialisers that will output a number like `5.0` as `5` to save space. Additionally, floating point numbers have a larger range than integers, so parsing them as integers can cause overflow errors.\r\n\r\nThe main problem is that Godot doesn't have a way to deserialise JSON as a type, which means you have to deal with the raw JSON data, which can be a problem in cases like this. However, I don't think that's a reason to deviate from the spec.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4185933442/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187224051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170#issuecomment-4187224051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118170","id":4187224051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75k_fz","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T14:49:24Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T14:49:24Z","body":"> have a way to deserialise JSON as a type, which means you have to deal with the raw JSON data\r\n\r\nSee https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_json.html#class-json-method-from-native","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187224051/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4199317816","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170#issuecomment-4199317816","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118170","id":4199317816,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76TIE4","user":{"login":"mashumafi","id":1059099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTkwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1059099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi","html_url":"https://github.com/mashumafi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T13:30:06Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T13:33:25Z","body":"@Joy-less I am not convinced\r\n\r\n> The JSON format [does not make a distinction between integers and floating point numbers](https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/reference/numeric#integer), so 1.0 is a valid way to represent an integer, and 1 is a valid way to represent a floating point number.\r\n\r\n`1` being a valid way to represent a float doesn't mean every number should be treated as float. There is documented distinction of integer and number types, it would be worth defining the distinction in any implementation.\r\n\r\n> There are plenty of JSON serialisers that will output a number like 5.0 as 5 to save space. \r\n\r\nI am only focused on deserializing here. Every parser out there includes some way to determine if a parsed value is an int vs float.\r\n\r\n> Additionally, floating point numbers have a larger range than integers, so parsing them as integers can cause overflow errors.\r\n\r\nLarger range but at the cost of precision. You get about 16 significant digits for a float. For `int64` you get 24 digits meaning you can represent larger numbers with higher resolution. For example parsing a number like `12345678901234567` would not work with the current implementation.\r\n\r\n> The main problem is that Godot doesn't have a way to deserialise JSON as a type, which means you have to deal with the raw JSON data, which can be a problem in cases like this. However, I don't think that's a reason to deviate from the spec.\r\n\r\nLook at other text parsing in Godot and how consistent they are with parsing int shaped text.\r\n\r\n*ConfigFile*\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar config := ConfigFile.new()\r\nconfig.parse(\"test=5\")\r\nprint(config.get_value(\"\", \"test\")) # prints \"5\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n*Expression*\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar expr := Expression.new()\r\nexpr.parse(\"5\")\r\nprint(expr.execute()) # prints \"5\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n*GDScript*\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar value : int = 5\r\nprint(value) # prints \"5\"\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4199317816/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4199609122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170#issuecomment-4199609122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118170","id":4199609122,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76UPMi","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T14:12:16Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T14:12:48Z","body":"Looking at JSON's [RFC](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8259#section-6), it only specifies that 1.0 and 1 are parsed as \"number\" but it doesn't require that they're both floats.\n\nLooking at [Ruby](https://onecompiler.com/ruby/44jnpugby) and [Python](https://www.online-python.com/oZrOaiXcI3), they both parse 1.0 as a float and 1 as an integer.\n\nLooks like it would be valid for GDScript to parse 1 as an integer, but it's not required by the spec. It would also be a breaking change.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4199609122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4199636766","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170#issuecomment-4199636766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118170","id":4199636766,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76UV8e","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":4